From: oliveagle <oliveagle@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 00:49:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(codex-client): honor Retry-After header for 429
 responses

- Add `backoff_for()` and `retry_after_from_err()` to parse Retry-After
- Support multiple header formats: Retry-After (sec/HTTP-date),
  X-RateLimit-Reset-After, X-RateLimit-Reset (unix)
- Add MAX_RETRY_AFTER cap (60s) to prevent excessive waits
- Add httpdate dependency and unit tests for all header formats
- Replace `backoff()` calls with `backoff_for()` in retry loop

This ensures codex respects server-provided backoff delays for rate
limits instead of blind exponential backoff.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
